WEBVTT

00:04.440 --> 00:06.680
TOMMY: Oh, there's a woman.

00:08.480 --> 00:09.480
Yeah.

00:10.920 --> 00:11.920
A woman.

00:14.120 --> 00:15.520
Who I love.

00:17.680 --> 00:19.120
And I got close.

00:30.640 --> 00:32.439
In the bleak midwinter...

00:37.520 --> 00:39.480
At some point in the near future,

00:39.560 --> 00:41.880
Mr. Churchill will want to speak to you
in person.

00:42.680 --> 00:43.800
Mr. Shelby,

00:45.160 --> 00:46.680
he has a job for you.

00:46.800 --> 00:48.240
(PANTING)

00:48.320 --> 00:49.560
We will be in touch.

01:10.080 --> 01:12.080
(THEME SONG PLAYING)

01:20.760 --> 01:22.640
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

01:24.320 --> 01:25.960
Oh, thank you.

01:38.960 --> 01:40.480
-(BABY CRYING)
-I'm going to take him.

01:48.920 --> 01:50.400
Some of us know the words.

02:19.600 --> 02:20.960
Trot on.

02:23.680 --> 02:28.040
(SINGING) In the bleak mid-winter

02:28.120 --> 02:32.640
Frosty wind made moan

02:32.720 --> 02:36.600
Earth stood hard as iron

02:36.680 --> 02:38.000
Trot on.

02:38.080 --> 02:39.720
Water like a stone

02:39.800 --> 02:40.800
Trot on.

02:42.760 --> 02:47.640
Snow had fallen, snow on snow

02:47.720 --> 02:51.560
Snow on snow

02:52.800 --> 02:57.480
In the bleak mid-winter

02:57.560 --> 03:01.760
Long ago

03:11.240 --> 03:13.000
(TRUMPETS BLOWING)

03:15.440 --> 03:17.000
(WEDDING MUSIC PLAYING)

03:17.080 --> 03:20.120
Here come the fucking cavalry.
Late as usual.

04:06.360 --> 04:08.120
JEREMIAH: Dearly beloved.

04:08.200 --> 04:12.560
We are gathered here today
to join together in holy matrimony

04:13.080 --> 04:16.959
Thomas Michael Shelby
and Grace Helen Burgess.

04:17.240 --> 04:19.320
(MUSIC PLAYING)

04:29.240 --> 04:30.240
(INDISTINCT)

04:35.520 --> 04:36.520
(INDISTINCT)

04:42.240 --> 04:44.160
JEREMIAH:
Do you, Thomas Michael Shelby,

04:44.880 --> 04:48.000
take Grace Helen Burgess
to be your lawful wedded wife?

04:49.600 --> 04:50.680
TOMMY: I do.

04:52.440 --> 04:54.640
Do you, Grace Helen Burgess,

04:54.720 --> 04:58.120
solemnly swear to love, honor,

04:58.200 --> 05:01.640
and obey till death do you part?

05:01.720 --> 05:02.760
GRACE: I do.

05:02.840 --> 05:06.080
JEREMIAH: I now pronounce you
husband and wife.

05:13.520 --> 05:15.400
(ALL CHEERING)

05:33.960 --> 05:35.160
Get out of it!

05:35.240 --> 05:36.920
(ALL TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

05:44.120 --> 05:46.640
-Go on, take the photograph!
-(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

06:01.400 --> 06:03.440
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

06:09.280 --> 06:10.280
Tommy.

06:12.440 --> 06:15.600
Arthur, get the bastards in the house.

06:15.680 --> 06:20.400
I will. I will. John! John-Boy!
Get 'em in the house, all of 'em.

06:23.160 --> 06:25.200
Go on, all of you! Back to the house!
Go on!

06:25.840 --> 06:27.560
(ALL CHEERING)

06:30.360 --> 06:32.120
(MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING)

06:52.440 --> 06:54.360
(ALL CHEERING AND APPLAUDING)

07:04.840 --> 07:06.880
(BALLROOM MUSIC PLAYING)

07:31.040 --> 07:34.360
All right, Pol. Tell the Lee girls
I've counted all the paintings.

07:34.440 --> 07:37.320
And, Pol, some people here
are not on the list.

07:39.760 --> 07:41.760
Curly, Charlie. Kitchen.

07:41.840 --> 07:43.800
-Time?
-Five minutes.

07:43.880 --> 07:46.840
Actually, we were told on the train
there'd be cocaine.

07:47.920 --> 07:50.480
Jeremiah, John-Boy, kitchen, let's go.

07:50.560 --> 07:53.280
I swear to God them fucking Cavalry boys
are asking for it.

07:53.360 --> 07:56.560
Uh, I was told to ask someone young.
Will there be cocaine?

07:56.640 --> 08:00.080
Sweetheart, I am young, informed
and, uh, very well-equipped.

08:00.160 --> 08:01.600
You chose your man wisely.

08:02.640 --> 08:04.440
Go on, kitchen now.

08:04.520 --> 08:06.400
Arthur, this lady
wants to play in the snow.

08:06.480 --> 08:09.000
No, no snow today. No snow today.

08:11.200 --> 08:12.840
Kitchen, come on.

08:12.920 --> 08:14.680
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

08:16.640 --> 08:18.360
(ALL LAUGHING)

08:21.120 --> 08:23.280
I just wish Tommy was here.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.520
-Where are they?
-JOHNNY: I don't know, Tommy.

08:41.600 --> 08:42.919
-Arthur, John, where are they?
-I don't know.

08:43.000 --> 08:45.800
-I am telling you now, we got lost.
-Come on.

08:45.880 --> 08:48.640
You really need to do a map. Thomas.

08:56.680 --> 08:59.160
Right, boys, you're all here.

09:01.880 --> 09:04.800
Today, this is my fucking wedding day.

09:04.880 --> 09:07.320
Yeah, and you said
there'd be no bloody uniforms.

09:07.400 --> 09:10.000
Nevertheless... Nevertheless, John...

09:10.080 --> 09:12.360
Despite the bad blood,

09:12.440 --> 09:14.240
I'll have none of it on my carpet.

09:14.320 --> 09:17.360
Now for Grace's sake,
nothing will go wrong.

09:17.440 --> 09:21.080
Those bastards out there are her family.

09:21.160 --> 09:25.560
And if you fuckers do anything
to embarrass her,

09:25.640 --> 09:31.120
your kin, your cousins, your horses,
your fucking kids, you do anything...

09:31.200 --> 09:32.880
-JOHN: Tom?
-To... What?

09:32.960 --> 09:33.960
What about snow?

09:34.520 --> 09:36.720
Yeah, their women are sports,
I'll say that...

09:36.800 --> 09:38.720
No. No. No.

09:40.040 --> 09:41.200
No cocaine.

09:42.440 --> 09:44.480
No cocaine. No sport.

09:44.560 --> 09:46.920
No telling fortunes. No racing.

09:47.000 --> 09:50.880
No fucking sucking petrol
out of their fucking cars.

09:52.480 --> 09:55.800
And, you, Charlie,
stop spinning yarns about me, eh?

09:55.880 --> 09:57.920
I'm just trying to sell you to them, Tom.

09:59.560 --> 10:00.720
But the main thing is,

10:01.560 --> 10:02.920
you bunch of fuckers,

10:03.480 --> 10:06.320
despite the provocation from the cavalry,

10:07.040 --> 10:08.240
no fighting.

10:09.440 --> 10:10.440
Oi!

10:12.040 --> 10:13.240
No fighting.

10:13.320 --> 10:14.440
No fucking fighting.

10:15.120 --> 10:16.120
No fighting.

10:17.080 --> 10:20.600
(SHOUTING) No fucking fighting!

10:22.360 --> 10:23.360
Good.

10:23.800 --> 10:26.040
-Get the fuck off me!
-(GLASS SHATTERS)

10:33.120 --> 10:34.440
You're needed downstairs.

10:34.680 --> 10:35.960
(CLEARS THROAT)

10:38.600 --> 10:40.280
Grace, you're needed downstairs.

10:40.360 --> 10:41.560
People are hungry.

10:42.400 --> 10:44.400
I was putting Charles to sleep. (SIGHS)

10:45.000 --> 10:47.000
I'll come down,
but not with you like this.

10:47.080 --> 10:48.200
All right, fine.

10:49.280 --> 10:50.440
GRACE: Tommy.

10:52.080 --> 10:56.240
I thought today was the reason
for the way you've been acting lately.

10:56.320 --> 10:58.600
I know there's business on your mind.

11:00.200 --> 11:02.240
-And I know there always will be.
-Yeah.

11:02.320 --> 11:04.800
Look, I am sorry
that they wore their uniforms.

11:04.880 --> 11:07.720
Yeah, they fucking did, eh.
They fucking did.

11:07.800 --> 11:09.480
But I can tell it's more than that.

11:11.840 --> 11:13.800
You've been like this for weeks.

11:16.040 --> 11:17.360
(CLEARS THROAT)

11:18.480 --> 11:20.720
I need you to tell me

11:21.480 --> 11:23.480
that it's business making you like this.

11:23.560 --> 11:25.480
And not regret over me.

11:26.720 --> 11:28.320
Say it out loud
and I'll know if it's true.

11:29.680 --> 11:31.000
(CLICKS TONGUE)

11:33.280 --> 11:34.720
It's business, Grace.

11:37.480 --> 11:39.600
And bad, bad business it is, all around.

11:45.280 --> 11:47.280
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

11:47.360 --> 11:49.000
And I'm scared, Grace.

11:50.400 --> 11:51.920
I'm scared for you.

11:52.000 --> 11:53.560
I'm scared for the baby.

11:54.000 --> 11:55.200
And this is how I am when I'm scared.

11:55.280 --> 11:57.400
It is unfamiliar to you, but not to me.

11:57.480 --> 12:02.320
I can... I can fucking be scared
and carry on.

12:06.400 --> 12:09.280
And it's not pleasant to look at
and no joy to be around.

12:10.960 --> 12:12.320
All right?

12:15.400 --> 12:17.560
I'm sorry. (SNIFFLES)

12:24.520 --> 12:26.600
We've just made vows to share everything.

12:29.000 --> 12:31.160
Tell me what it is you're afraid of.

12:41.240 --> 12:43.360
-(MUSIC PLAYING)
-(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

12:55.160 --> 12:56.560
-Stand up. Stand up, stand up.
-Don't.

13:00.080 --> 13:01.240
Arthur's speech.

13:02.800 --> 13:04.480
I'm scared of fucking Arthur's speech.

13:07.960 --> 13:09.080
All right?

13:10.400 --> 13:11.720
Me, too.

13:15.400 --> 13:17.120
Tommy, what are you doing?

13:17.200 --> 13:18.240
Tommy.

13:18.320 --> 13:22.200
There's half the British Army
waiting for us downstairs.

13:22.720 --> 13:27.080
They're King's Irish.
We waited two weeks in the mud for them.

13:28.520 --> 13:30.640
Tommy. (CHUCKLES)

13:32.400 --> 13:36.400
There are things, that if I take them off,
I won't be able to put back on...

13:36.480 --> 13:38.440
-That's good.
-(CHUCKLES)

13:45.760 --> 13:47.320
Hello, Mrs. Shelby.

13:48.440 --> 13:51.360
-I'm sorry for being busy in my head.
-(CHUCKLES)

13:53.520 --> 13:55.360
Now let's complete the ceremony.

13:57.440 --> 13:59.320
Hey, Vincent, Vincent, Vincent.

13:59.400 --> 14:02.720
What do you call an animal
with a prick halfway up its back?

14:03.440 --> 14:05.640
A cavalry horse. (LAUGHING)

14:06.400 --> 14:07.880
He got... He gets it.

14:10.600 --> 14:12.440
Fuck it. Fuck it.

14:12.520 --> 14:14.680
Where the bloody hell are they?
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

14:14.760 --> 14:17.560
You're best man, Arthur. Go and find them.

14:19.480 --> 14:20.640
Yeah.

14:21.960 --> 14:23.440
ADA: That's completely nonsense.

14:23.520 --> 14:26.560
You know, we're part of a serious
political movement and organization.

14:26.640 --> 14:29.960
They're not "secret little meetings,"
they're just meetings.

14:30.040 --> 14:32.160
We talk about the world,
about the people in it,

14:32.240 --> 14:35.120
about our current political landscape
and what's going on.

14:35.200 --> 14:37.240
You know, we really need to re-evaluate
the way our government...

14:37.320 --> 14:38.880
(WHISPERING INDISTINCTLY)

14:41.200 --> 14:43.640
-POLLY: Very strange indeed.
-He's looking over.

14:43.720 --> 14:44.720
What?

14:47.040 --> 14:49.000
He's coming. He bloody is.

14:51.040 --> 14:52.200
Fuck. It's the wrong one.

14:53.760 --> 14:55.440
What do you mean "the wrong one"?
How many are there?

14:55.520 --> 14:57.120
There's two, giving me the eye.

14:57.200 --> 14:59.160
I prefer the other one. He looks harmless.

15:01.840 --> 15:04.760
It must be that bloody lipstick
Tommy brought you back from New York.

15:09.280 --> 15:11.840
I couldn't help noticing
you are unaccompanied.

15:11.920 --> 15:15.480
I also am alone. May I join you?

15:23.840 --> 15:26.360
ARTHUR: Tommy?
Oh. (SNIFFLES)

15:27.040 --> 15:30.800
Didn't see a thing. Did not see a thing.
Sorry, brother.

15:31.840 --> 15:33.280
I need you downstairs.

15:33.880 --> 15:35.360
It's all right. We're done. (SIGHS)

15:35.440 --> 15:36.640
-You good?
-Yeah.

15:36.720 --> 15:38.080
-Never been better.
-Yeah?

15:38.160 --> 15:39.760
-Are you drunk?
-Huh? No.

15:40.560 --> 15:41.560
No.

15:43.520 --> 15:44.520
Here.

15:47.880 --> 15:49.920
All right, it's just one drink, then.

15:50.440 --> 15:52.240
Linda's a good woman, Arthur.

15:56.880 --> 15:58.040
Good whiskey.

15:59.560 --> 16:01.840
A good man needs to
hold out sometimes, eh?

16:07.160 --> 16:08.480
(SIGHS)

16:08.920 --> 16:13.360
So, uh, do I mention this
in my speech, then, eh?

16:13.440 --> 16:15.960
Not unless you want to get cut, Arthur.

16:16.040 --> 16:17.360
ARTHUR: Sorry, sister.

16:18.560 --> 16:19.960
TOMMY: Right. Look.

16:20.680 --> 16:22.640
Tell the maids to break out the champagne.

16:22.720 --> 16:24.080
We'll be down in a minute.

16:24.160 --> 16:26.160
Champagne, yeah. Okay.

16:27.000 --> 16:29.360
-I got it right here. I'm ready.
-Good. Good.

16:33.680 --> 16:35.240
Where are you from?

16:40.840 --> 16:41.880
I'm a refugee.

16:43.600 --> 16:44.600
From where?

16:50.160 --> 16:51.400
Russia.

16:53.640 --> 16:54.720
In the past few months,

16:54.800 --> 16:57.600
Thomas has developed
some business interests with Russia.

16:59.640 --> 17:01.680
I see he has confided in you.

17:04.079 --> 17:05.119
Hmm.

17:05.200 --> 17:07.720
You need his permission
to even speak to me.

17:11.359 --> 17:14.000
My senior position
within the Shelby company

17:14.079 --> 17:17.720
means I don't often have to ask permission
from anyone

17:17.800 --> 17:19.200
to do anything.

17:19.880 --> 17:21.640
So perhaps you'll just tell me

17:21.720 --> 17:26.160
why the fuck you're talking
Russian business on Thomas's wedding day.

17:27.880 --> 17:29.000
LIZZIE: Hold on, wait a second.

17:29.080 --> 17:31.680
-So you're saying I'm not allowed a man...
-It's about your choice of man.

17:31.760 --> 17:32.920
LIZZIE: I'm not allowed a man on my arm?

17:33.000 --> 17:34.440
MICHAEL: Thomas says
that they're the rules.

17:34.520 --> 17:36.440
LIZZIE: Fucking parish bastard!

17:36.520 --> 17:38.920
Michael, speeches. Come on.

17:39.000 --> 17:41.840
Arthur. You know
why he didn't come, don't you?

17:41.920 --> 17:43.280
Why who didn't come?

17:43.360 --> 17:44.760
My bloody man.

17:44.840 --> 17:46.360
Oh, you mean the wop?

17:46.440 --> 17:50.640
LIZZIE: I just heard there was a fire
at his restaurant midnight last night.

17:50.720 --> 17:53.160
And a smashed back window
and a smell of petrol.

17:53.800 --> 17:56.360
Lizzie, we tried to talk some sense
into you.

17:56.880 --> 17:58.160
We did checks on him.

17:58.240 --> 18:00.160
He's had five different names
in the last six years,

18:00.240 --> 18:01.880
and he's got connections
with the Naples boys.

18:01.960 --> 18:02.960
ARTHUR: Come on, Michael.

18:03.040 --> 18:04.440
What do you know about love?

18:04.520 --> 18:06.320
About when lightning strikes.

18:06.400 --> 18:10.160
So, it was lightning, hmm? Not petrol.

18:11.240 --> 18:12.520
I thought you were
off the whiskey, Arthur.

18:12.600 --> 18:16.480
Yeah, I am. Having a couple now and again
to remind myself why I don't drink it.

18:16.560 --> 18:17.600
(CHUCKLES)

18:17.680 --> 18:20.600
You set fire to his restaurant
to stop him coming.

18:20.680 --> 18:23.880
You have no right to choose
who I step out with in my own time!

18:28.600 --> 18:30.000
(MICHAEL CLEARS THROAT)

18:34.720 --> 18:39.640
Lizzie, you now have an important position
in this company.

18:40.720 --> 18:43.760
You got the order, same as us.

18:45.840 --> 18:47.560
You can do it.

18:52.280 --> 18:54.400
Until further notice...

18:55.440 --> 18:57.840
No fraternizing with the foreigners.

19:01.560 --> 19:03.080
Yeah, well, you can tell Tommy from me

19:03.160 --> 19:05.800
all the girls in the office think
he's losing his fucking mind!

19:11.200 --> 19:12.240
To the bride.

19:12.880 --> 19:14.120
ALL: The bride.

19:14.200 --> 19:15.640
-The bride.
-The bride.

19:18.440 --> 19:22.680
And now, (CLEARS THROAT)
according to tradition,

19:22.760 --> 19:25.160
my best man will say a few words.

19:25.360 --> 19:30.240
Go on! Here he goes! Go on, Arthur!

19:34.560 --> 19:37.760
Right, um... I'm not one for speeches.

19:37.840 --> 19:40.080
-Sing, then!
-ARTHUR: I will later, John.

19:41.480 --> 19:44.080
But, uh, I do, uh...

19:45.080 --> 19:47.840
I do have some words written down here

19:49.720 --> 19:51.360
on this piece of paper.

19:52.680 --> 19:57.560
This doesn't include everything
that I want to say.

19:57.640 --> 19:59.760
Arthur, just, uh...
Just read what we wrote down, eh?

20:00.960 --> 20:04.120
-I will, I will.
-Mmm-hmm.

20:04.200 --> 20:05.440
But...

20:06.480 --> 20:10.800
First... First, uh, a few words from...
From the heart.

20:14.640 --> 20:15.640
Um...

20:17.160 --> 20:19.800
This man here, my brother Tommy,

20:20.960 --> 20:25.160
helped me survive through
some of the worst times.

20:25.280 --> 20:26.880
(COUGHS AND CLEARS THROAT)

20:26.960 --> 20:29.040
It's a wedding, Arthur, tell a joke.

20:29.120 --> 20:30.280
JOHN: Yeah, tell a joke.

20:30.880 --> 20:33.200
What I am trying to say is that...

20:34.960 --> 20:39.520
(STUTTERS) My brother
and the love of a good woman

20:40.840 --> 20:43.000
pulled me through that time.

20:44.600 --> 20:48.680
Now Tommy also
has the love of a good woman.

20:50.240 --> 20:52.080
Her name's Grace.

20:53.640 --> 20:55.880
Like the grace of the good Lord.

20:58.840 --> 20:59.840
And even though

21:01.520 --> 21:05.840
the circumstances of their union
was tragic...

21:05.920 --> 21:08.200
All right. Let's, uh... Arthur.

21:08.280 --> 21:10.320
Let's raise a toast, eh?

21:10.400 --> 21:12.120
To, uh... (CLEARS THROAT)

21:12.200 --> 21:15.760
To love, to peace, to marriage.

21:15.840 --> 21:17.560
-And to marriage.
-To marriage.

21:23.400 --> 21:27.920
JOHN: Well done, Arthur, beautiful speech.
Really nice.

21:29.760 --> 21:31.040
Really, really nice.

21:38.000 --> 21:40.160
Where is he fucking going?

21:44.800 --> 21:47.240
-I think I messed it up.
-No, not a bit.

21:47.640 --> 21:50.040
-Hmm.
-You spoke with such truth.

21:51.080 --> 21:52.560
And God heard you.

21:52.640 --> 21:54.280
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

21:55.480 --> 21:58.240
TOMMY: Can I have a word
with my brother, please, Linda?

21:58.800 --> 22:01.760
-What he was going to say was beautiful.
-Mmm-hmm.

22:02.480 --> 22:03.880
Alone, please.

22:09.720 --> 22:11.000
All right. Come here.

22:12.240 --> 22:13.280
Come here.

22:15.160 --> 22:16.640
(TOMMY SIGHS)

22:17.960 --> 22:19.960
We talked about this, Arthur.

22:20.040 --> 22:21.840
That's why we wrote it all down.

22:22.960 --> 22:26.840
Most of Grace's side don't even know
her husband killed himself.

22:26.920 --> 22:28.120
They think it was an accident.

22:29.120 --> 22:30.400
-Oh, I know.
-You know.

22:31.600 --> 22:32.800
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

22:32.880 --> 22:34.440
What do you think I am? Hmm?

22:36.040 --> 22:38.080
What do you think I am, Tommy, eh?

22:38.640 --> 22:41.600
-You think I'm a fucking idiot, don't you?
-All right, boys.

22:41.680 --> 22:44.840
-Come on, have a good night.
-You think I would say it...

22:44.920 --> 22:47.520
-Come on, then. That's okay.
-You keep walking, you nosy bastards.

22:47.600 --> 22:50.240
-Arthur. Fucking hell.
-All right. You stay away from me.

22:50.320 --> 22:52.240
You stay away from me. I've had enough.

22:55.600 --> 22:56.600
Ah!

22:56.960 --> 22:58.000
Shit.

22:58.520 --> 23:00.400
-(GROANING)
-Yeah. Yeah.

23:09.440 --> 23:10.880
Ah, shit.

23:12.720 --> 23:15.200
Three shots I've had, that's it.

23:15.280 --> 23:16.920
-TOMMY: I know.
-I drew the line.

23:17.000 --> 23:18.040
I know.

23:18.120 --> 23:20.600
I know you've turned a corner, Arthur.

23:20.680 --> 23:22.000
-Yeah.
-I know.

23:22.080 --> 23:23.120
-Yeah.
-Mmm-hmm.

23:23.200 --> 23:24.480
-I'm your best man.
-I know.

23:25.520 --> 23:27.000
I wasn't going to tell no one.

23:27.080 --> 23:28.280
(WHISPERS) It's all right.

23:29.080 --> 23:31.040
It's done. Get up. Get up.

23:31.760 --> 23:32.920
-Get up.
-(GROANS)

23:34.120 --> 23:35.240
Right.

23:36.400 --> 23:39.280
The Russians have made contact.

23:39.800 --> 23:42.000
We have to get used to
how these bastards operate.

23:42.520 --> 23:43.600
For them,

23:43.680 --> 23:46.080
family is a weakness,
and they go after them.

23:46.160 --> 23:49.600
For me, family is my strength.
And there's business to be done.

23:49.680 --> 23:51.480
And I need you.

23:51.560 --> 23:53.800
Now, fuck speeches, fuck weddings.

23:54.320 --> 23:56.640
You're my best man every fucking day.

23:58.120 --> 23:59.760
-Okay.
-Yeah.

24:00.320 --> 24:02.880
Now go and get John, get him sobered up.

24:02.960 --> 24:04.360
Find Johnny Dogs.

24:04.440 --> 24:06.840
It's the Russians
through the smoke tonight.

24:08.800 --> 24:10.240
All right.

24:10.320 --> 24:11.400
Good.

24:14.600 --> 24:15.600
And, Arthur?

24:18.200 --> 24:21.600
In future, it's not always right
to listen to Linda.

24:22.360 --> 24:23.520
-Yeah? Yeah.
-Yeah.

24:29.080 --> 24:31.040
-(MUSIC PLAYING)
-(PEOPLE LAUGHING)

24:32.280 --> 24:34.160
It's full of gypsies and blacks.

24:34.240 --> 24:37.360
Grace says he exports automobiles
to the colonies.

24:41.080 --> 24:42.680
TOMMY: Pol, now.

24:47.640 --> 24:48.960
So what does he say?

24:50.000 --> 24:52.520
He won't meet you
unless you give us the name.

24:52.600 --> 24:54.200
What name?

24:54.280 --> 24:57.440
We were told to ask for a code name
when contact was made.

25:00.240 --> 25:03.360
Constantine. The code is Constantine.

25:11.960 --> 25:14.160
Tommy said no racing, no gambling.

25:14.240 --> 25:15.880
Yeah, he's changed his mind.

25:15.960 --> 25:18.160
-Right. Don't worry Finn, okay?
-Right. (CHUCKLES)

25:18.240 --> 25:20.240
Cavalry boys ride like a sack of stones,
all right?

25:20.320 --> 25:23.840
John. John, there's an awful lot of
King's shillings around here today.

25:23.920 --> 25:26.280
Now, out of loyalty to the regiment,

25:26.360 --> 25:28.440
they'll all be putting their money
on this bad boy

25:28.520 --> 25:31.520
-that I filled up with morphine and water.
-(BOTH LAUGHING)

25:31.600 --> 25:34.520
Here. Tommy's all right if I, uh,
do the book, is he?

25:34.600 --> 25:39.000
He said betting's okay, but all proceeds
go to the Shelby Foundation charity.

25:39.080 --> 25:41.160
Oh, is this charity of his for real, then?

25:41.240 --> 25:44.120
He says he wants to be seen
giving back to the poor of Birmingham.

25:44.200 --> 25:45.800
So that'll be me, John.

25:45.880 --> 25:48.320
Myself.
If I can't earn a shilling here tonight.

25:48.400 --> 25:49.440
Huh?

25:49.520 --> 25:51.800
They'll make him
the fucking Lord Mayor next.

25:51.880 --> 25:53.680
Mmm, that's the idea, Charlie-Boy.

25:54.240 --> 25:55.560
Fucking hell.

25:55.640 --> 25:59.200
Right, all you lot
make as much noise and fuss as you can.

25:59.280 --> 26:00.680
Especially fucking you.

26:00.760 --> 26:02.360
So we're a fucking distraction, John,
is it?

26:02.440 --> 26:03.480
-(BOTH LAUGHING)
-Huh?

26:03.560 --> 26:06.680
Tommy is doing business on a night
he should be just fucking.

26:06.760 --> 26:08.480
(LAUGHING)

26:08.560 --> 26:10.760
Right, place your bets with me.

26:10.840 --> 26:12.880
Your favorites. Your favorites.

26:12.960 --> 26:14.000
Come on, boys.

26:14.080 --> 26:17.560
'Cause I hope my boy Finn
doesn't fall off that fucking horse.

26:18.040 --> 26:19.120
Come on.

26:19.200 --> 26:20.200
For charity.

26:20.600 --> 26:21.800
CURLY: Shut up.

26:26.720 --> 26:28.000
ARTHUR: Oh, you found it.

26:28.640 --> 26:29.840
We nearly gave up.

26:38.760 --> 26:41.240
Did he tell you
what my business with him is?

26:47.000 --> 26:48.680
The same shit the Turks used to smoke.

26:50.320 --> 26:51.360
I wonder,

26:51.880 --> 26:54.320
why does he trust his aunt
more than his brothers?

26:55.400 --> 26:56.920
(CHUCKLES)

26:59.680 --> 27:01.400
TOMMY: Go and watch the race, boys.

27:03.480 --> 27:04.960
The Turk's clean.

27:07.520 --> 27:09.280
I am Russian.

27:10.000 --> 27:11.720
Same fucking thing.

27:32.600 --> 27:34.840
So you make contact on my wedding day.

27:34.920 --> 27:36.880
You now have very powerful enemies.

27:37.880 --> 27:40.680
At the Soviet Embassy
and within your own government.

27:40.760 --> 27:42.200
You are being watched,

27:42.280 --> 27:46.240
at your house, your office, your clubs,

27:46.960 --> 27:48.360
your bars.

27:48.440 --> 27:51.240
You best be quick or I'll be missed.
Now where's the money?

27:51.320 --> 27:53.680
The Duke's niece is
bringing it from London.

27:55.680 --> 27:57.480
I was told money on contact.

27:58.160 --> 28:00.520
Ten thousand in US dollars.

28:01.720 --> 28:04.720
My employer only trusts
members of his family with cash.

28:05.640 --> 28:07.680
She will be at Snow Hill station at 10:00.

28:07.840 --> 28:09.160
(CHUCKLES)

28:10.200 --> 28:15.560
A woman alone in Birmingham
with $10,000 in cash.

28:16.320 --> 28:18.400
-And she also has a revolver.
-Oh, I see.

28:18.480 --> 28:20.080
I thought you trusted women.

28:20.160 --> 28:22.080
I don't trust Birmingham.

28:22.160 --> 28:23.880
I'll have her picked up.

28:23.960 --> 28:26.320
-By who?
-By the police, pal.

28:27.120 --> 28:28.400
This is our city.

28:37.520 --> 28:39.280
(ALL CHEERING)

28:49.680 --> 28:51.680
ARTHUR: Fucking beautiful horse, Tom.

28:53.440 --> 28:54.480
Beautiful.

28:55.520 --> 28:57.280
-He's a natural, that boy.
-Yeah.

28:57.360 --> 28:59.560
Good posture. Rides like Dad.

28:59.640 --> 29:00.680
TOMMY: All right, listen to me.

29:00.760 --> 29:04.680
Tell Johnny Dogs and his boys
to light a fire in the woods,

29:04.760 --> 29:06.520
a big one, to take meat.

29:07.600 --> 29:09.520
And send Finn to watch the gates.

29:09.600 --> 29:11.280
Moss is bringing someone.

29:17.640 --> 29:18.800
CHARLOTTE: You don't?

29:21.360 --> 29:24.040
I just needed to bring you somewhere
nobody could see.

29:24.120 --> 29:26.720
But your friend gave this to me.
He said you all did it.

29:27.600 --> 29:28.800
Not me.

29:28.880 --> 29:31.000
But it's all right. Go on.

29:37.040 --> 29:38.160
(MICHAEL CHUCKLES)

29:38.240 --> 29:39.680
I see you don't, either.

29:40.720 --> 29:43.240
-Don't be silly, everyone does.
-So go on, then.

29:43.400 --> 29:46.240
-(SIGHS) Cut the snow.
-We call it Tokyo.

29:46.320 --> 29:48.280
We call it whatever the customer calls it.

29:49.000 --> 29:52.400
In London,
we were told you are all gangsters.

29:52.960 --> 29:56.000
So that's why you got on the train
to dirty, old Birmingham.

29:57.320 --> 29:59.000
For a dirty, old night.

30:02.400 --> 30:03.960
You don't look like the others.

30:04.040 --> 30:05.360
That's the idea.

30:06.560 --> 30:09.000
I put it all together,
but I don't partake.

30:10.440 --> 30:13.280
You see, I've got a bright future,
you see.

30:15.920 --> 30:17.160
Mapped out.

30:22.360 --> 30:24.600
But you want me to be like them,
don't you?

30:31.160 --> 30:33.800
There's a cavalry officer
stationed in Ceylon.

30:33.880 --> 30:37.000
And when his tour of duty ends in March,
we'll be engaged.

30:38.800 --> 30:42.280
So I have a bright future, too.

30:43.280 --> 30:44.680
Mapped out.

30:45.600 --> 30:47.640
But you want to try things first.

30:57.760 --> 30:59.040
(SNORTS)

31:00.760 --> 31:02.200
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

31:09.640 --> 31:11.080
No. Keep it.

31:12.520 --> 31:13.920
As if I were a whore.

31:18.520 --> 31:21.080
Well, if that's the game you want to play.

31:36.040 --> 31:38.200
(PEOPLE LAUGHING
AND TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

31:43.000 --> 31:44.120
Polly.

31:44.920 --> 31:46.000
Hello, Grace.

31:48.000 --> 31:50.560
You look absolutely beautiful.

31:52.920 --> 31:54.520
Welcome to the family.

31:57.160 --> 31:58.960
Oh, I see. Tommy's orders.

31:59.960 --> 32:01.200
No upsets tonight.

32:01.280 --> 32:04.640
Your hair, everything, beautiful.

32:06.560 --> 32:07.800
Do you know where he is?

32:08.560 --> 32:11.320
Yes. Yes, I do.

32:13.280 --> 32:16.960
You know, Tommy really wants to keep
certain things a secret from me.

32:18.520 --> 32:20.440
It's very hard when you're man and wife.

32:20.920 --> 32:23.640
We were late coming down
because we were having sex.

32:24.120 --> 32:25.960
So afterwards, he told me everything.

32:28.920 --> 32:33.080
Royalist Russians buying weapons
to fight the Bolsheviks in Georgia.

32:35.200 --> 32:36.960
A lost cause, Tommy says.

32:38.280 --> 32:40.720
And Churchill, that he's the go-between.

32:40.800 --> 32:44.480
But it's against government policy
so everything must be kept a secret.

32:51.080 --> 32:52.200
You know it's begun?

32:55.480 --> 32:57.600
They started the business tonight?

33:02.920 --> 33:04.120
No. (SIGHS)

33:06.040 --> 33:07.320
I didn't.

33:09.200 --> 33:11.000
But you just told me.

33:11.080 --> 33:12.520
So, thank you.

33:15.920 --> 33:18.400
Let's not forget
I used to do this for a living.

33:20.720 --> 33:22.520
Oh, I haven't forgotten, sweetheart.

33:24.240 --> 33:26.360
It's only Thomas that's forgotten
what you are.

33:26.440 --> 33:28.480
MAN: Ladies and Gentlemen.

33:29.240 --> 33:32.960
The bride and the groom
will now dance alone.

33:33.040 --> 33:34.760
(ALL CHEERING)

33:39.320 --> 33:41.160
(MUSIC PLAYING)

33:46.800 --> 33:49.600
Polly just told me
there is business being done.

33:53.200 --> 33:54.480
I didn't ask them to come.

33:56.720 --> 33:59.360
Tommy, please don't let
anything happen tonight.

34:03.600 --> 34:08.360
Just get this business done
and get away from things like this.

34:10.760 --> 34:12.239
I'll run the foundation,

34:13.560 --> 34:16.159
you'll run the tracks and sell cars.

34:20.639 --> 34:21.840
Promise me.

34:22.920 --> 34:23.960
Hmm?

34:24.880 --> 34:26.400
A wedding vow.

34:28.040 --> 34:29.320
I promise.

34:30.480 --> 34:32.080
No guns in the house

34:33.080 --> 34:35.320
-and Charles will never see one.
-(CHUCKLES)

34:36.960 --> 34:38.639
I love you, Thomas Shelby.

34:41.000 --> 34:42.280
You keep us safe.

34:43.199 --> 34:44.520
I love you.

34:45.600 --> 34:49.120
And I promise I will make us safe.

34:53.840 --> 34:56.760
MAN: Ladies and gentlemen,
you may now join.

35:11.920 --> 35:13.160
Gate house, come on.

35:25.640 --> 35:26.720
(ENGINE STOPS)

35:26.800 --> 35:31.520
Tommy, Arthur, Collins.

35:32.080 --> 35:36.280
May I introduce you to the
Grand Duchess Tatiana Petrovna,

35:37.800 --> 35:39.720
from Tbilisi, Georgia.

35:41.000 --> 35:45.480
Grand Duchess, may I introduce you
to the Shelby brothers.

35:46.040 --> 35:47.640
Small Heath, Birmingham.

35:50.600 --> 35:53.360
And, uh, good luck with this one, Tom.

35:58.480 --> 35:59.880
Give me the money.

36:01.440 --> 36:03.640
I was told to give it to Mr. Kaledin.

36:04.280 --> 36:07.320
Whoever it is up there,
he gave the wrong name.

36:08.640 --> 36:11.800
We asked him the name
and he gave the wrong one.

36:12.360 --> 36:14.520
-What name did he give?
-No.

36:16.600 --> 36:18.440
I don't trust any of you.

36:19.880 --> 36:21.360
Now you give me the money.

36:23.000 --> 36:26.880
I know Mr. Kaledin by sight from Tbilisi.
Is his hair dark?

36:26.960 --> 36:29.040
The instructions I was given

36:29.120 --> 36:33.520
was anyone using the wrong code name
was an infiltrator for the Soviet Embassy.

36:34.880 --> 36:35.920
Just let me go to the house.

36:36.000 --> 36:39.400
I do not want this shit
anywhere near my fucking house.

36:44.480 --> 36:46.960
All I know is "no variations."

36:47.840 --> 36:49.960
That's from Churchill himself.

36:50.040 --> 36:53.160
Whoever it is up at the house,
he gave the wrong fucking name.

36:56.440 --> 37:00.560
And you do this to me
on my fucking wedding day.

37:00.760 --> 37:01.800
(CLICKS TONGUE)

37:03.560 --> 37:05.600
The money is in the car, Mr. Shelby.

37:06.960 --> 37:08.400
Fetch it out and count it.

37:09.960 --> 37:12.280
Good. Finn.

37:18.040 --> 37:19.280
(COUGHS)

37:32.760 --> 37:35.080
Yeah. We're good.

37:36.440 --> 37:38.640
You can go. Moss... (CLEARS THROAT)

37:39.080 --> 37:40.120
Can you do it?

37:42.880 --> 37:44.240
Can you kill?

37:48.840 --> 37:53.840
Moss, you take the "Duchess"
back to Birmingham.

37:55.440 --> 37:56.520
MOSS: Right-o Tom.

37:58.200 --> 37:59.320
Come on, love.

38:02.440 --> 38:03.480
That's right.

38:07.280 --> 38:08.960
(PEOPLE LAUGHING)

38:11.000 --> 38:14.480
You have got to tell me the reason,
otherwise I'll never be able to trust you.

38:16.080 --> 38:17.600
The truth is,

38:19.920 --> 38:22.800
that I slept with the wife of
one of the colonels who sat for me.

38:23.960 --> 38:25.720
But that was 12 years ago.

38:27.840 --> 38:30.440
And the aristocracy
don't believe in forgiveness.

38:34.400 --> 38:36.040
Neither do the Shelbys.

38:44.520 --> 38:45.680
(ENGINE STOPS)

38:53.640 --> 38:54.960
So, we kill him?

38:55.680 --> 38:56.760
He's a red.

38:59.080 --> 39:02.480
We're being paid by the whites.
It's part of the contract.

39:02.560 --> 39:03.960
Contract.

39:07.560 --> 39:09.280
We should never have got into this, Tom.

39:10.600 --> 39:12.040
There was no choice.

39:14.000 --> 39:18.000
"A factory break-in,"
that's what you said.

39:18.080 --> 39:20.240
Yeah. And that's what it is.

39:22.360 --> 39:24.800
There's just some shit that goes with it.

39:32.520 --> 39:34.040
And who shovels it? Hmm?

39:36.880 --> 39:40.760
Who fucking shovels it? Eh?

39:42.320 --> 39:43.720
I fucking know.

39:44.640 --> 39:46.400
-Arthur?
-I fucking know.

39:46.480 --> 39:47.680
Arthur.

39:48.720 --> 39:51.640
There's 10 times where that's coming from,
10 times.

39:51.720 --> 39:53.640
For lifting vehicles
off a fucking shop floor.

39:53.720 --> 39:56.640
Vehicles, Tommy. Fucking vehicles.

39:56.720 --> 39:58.600
-Nothing about tanks.
-Yeah.

39:59.160 --> 40:03.000
Arthur, you listen to me.
You listen to me, all right?

40:03.080 --> 40:06.960
There are powerful people in this country
who want to help these mad bastards,

40:07.040 --> 40:10.600
including the King, Churchill
and half the fucking Tory Party.

40:10.680 --> 40:14.400
And if we refuse, Arthur,
if we fucking refuse,

40:14.960 --> 40:18.280
they will see to it
that we hang for one of our many sins.

40:18.360 --> 40:21.000
Now, we've never earned money
like this. Never.

40:21.880 --> 40:25.440
We'll use it to buy
the wharf at Boston docks.

40:25.520 --> 40:27.200
That's why I've asked for dollars.

40:28.760 --> 40:31.880
And when it's done,
it's business as usual.

40:39.160 --> 40:42.120
Come on, brother. It's my wedding night.

40:47.920 --> 40:49.600
(CHATTERING)

40:49.680 --> 40:52.000
-Where's John?
-Looking for Esme.

40:52.080 --> 40:53.160
Right.

40:53.800 --> 40:55.480
I'm Ruben Oliver, portrait artist.

40:56.080 --> 40:59.320
I really enjoyed the depiction of you
in the dining room.

40:59.720 --> 41:02.280
[In Romani] Johnny's lit a fire.
Keep people dancing.

41:10.240 --> 41:12.120
Nice to meet you, Mr. Oliver.

41:18.280 --> 41:19.640
Johnny, ragtime.

41:19.720 --> 41:21.360
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

42:12.240 --> 42:13.520
(SIGHS)

42:20.720 --> 42:22.160
So, where were we?

42:23.000 --> 42:26.080
-Crimea.
-Oh, I mean before I bored you with war.

42:26.160 --> 42:27.200
(CHUCKLES)

42:27.280 --> 42:29.080
-Politics.
-Ah, yes.

42:32.080 --> 42:35.040
You're the only one in your family
who is a communist?

42:35.800 --> 42:38.440
Some of them are,
they just don't know it.

42:38.520 --> 42:41.560
(CHUCKLES) And you are
a very close family, yes?

42:41.680 --> 42:44.360
Mmm, always within punching distance.

42:45.480 --> 42:46.760
What does that mean?

42:47.920 --> 42:50.000
It means, "Yeah, we're a close family."

42:55.040 --> 42:56.840
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

43:03.800 --> 43:04.840
Arthur?

43:06.920 --> 43:09.080
I do apologize for the interruption.

43:11.120 --> 43:13.760
There is a woman here
to see you, Mr. Kaledin.

43:14.680 --> 43:16.240
She just arrived.

43:30.680 --> 43:32.560
(LAUGHTER AND INDISTINCT TALKING)

43:38.920 --> 43:41.480
So, Tatiana made it from London safe?

43:41.560 --> 43:43.440
-Yes.
-Where is she?

43:43.520 --> 43:45.000
Out by the stables.

43:56.040 --> 43:57.680
Can I use the lavatory?

44:04.720 --> 44:10.200
You can piss outside by the stables.

44:24.240 --> 44:25.400
No!

44:26.040 --> 44:28.120
(SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

44:30.000 --> 44:31.640
(GROANING)

44:46.080 --> 44:48.000
(MEN TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

44:49.600 --> 44:51.160
Very sensible idea, Mr. Shelby.

44:52.160 --> 44:54.480
Clear the air away from the ladies.

44:54.880 --> 44:56.480
(GRUNTING)

44:57.120 --> 44:58.880
We are rather like generals here,
aren't we?

45:00.080 --> 45:02.080
Watching our men do battle.

45:02.160 --> 45:05.080
We are a bit too close to the fighting
to be generals, surely.

45:05.200 --> 45:06.680
(SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

45:08.320 --> 45:09.920
(PANTING)

45:16.640 --> 45:18.400
(SCREAMING)

45:28.440 --> 45:30.160
(TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

45:32.200 --> 45:36.280
You know, Mr. Shelby, some of us only
agreed to come today to bless this union

45:36.360 --> 45:38.960
because of your exemplary war record.

45:39.040 --> 45:41.240
But as Grace's uncle

45:41.320 --> 45:44.360
and a kind of father to her
for many years,

45:46.080 --> 45:48.400
I'm still deeply uneasy

45:49.480 --> 45:53.200
about the many stories of corruption
and violence.

45:54.280 --> 45:56.040
(BOTH STRUGGLING)

45:57.400 --> 45:58.960
(SCREAMING)

46:00.800 --> 46:03.320
Drink the fucking wine and smile.

46:04.640 --> 46:06.040
That's what I'm doing.

46:11.400 --> 46:13.440
ARTHUR: Oh, you got me good.

46:18.360 --> 46:20.400
Oh, you fucking bastard.

46:21.280 --> 46:23.160
(ALL SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

46:23.720 --> 46:24.880
No foul!

46:27.000 --> 46:28.040
No foul!

46:31.280 --> 46:33.040
(PANTING)

46:53.360 --> 46:54.800
KALEDIN: Don't shoot.

46:54.880 --> 46:56.000
No!

46:56.080 --> 46:57.360
Oh, for the love of God, don't shoot.

46:57.440 --> 46:59.160
No! No!

46:59.240 --> 47:00.480
-No!
-For the love of God...

47:00.560 --> 47:02.520
-No! No! No!
-For the love of God...

47:03.160 --> 47:04.360
-No!
-For the love of God.

47:05.120 --> 47:06.160
(GUNSHOT)

47:06.240 --> 47:08.240
-What was that?
-(BOTH PANTING)

47:08.320 --> 47:10.320
It's probably just a car back-firing.

47:10.680 --> 47:12.320
(PANTING)

47:49.760 --> 47:51.880
It wasn't the day I was expecting.

47:53.320 --> 47:54.520
Nor me.

47:58.480 --> 47:59.680
It's over now.

48:01.760 --> 48:03.480
Tomorrow it'll be just us.

48:09.120 --> 48:10.480
(SIGHS)

48:11.680 --> 48:12.800
Come here.

48:25.720 --> 48:27.520
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

48:27.600 --> 48:30.240
CURLY: Go on.
You've had a great night.

49:00.920 --> 49:02.320
The water froze in my car.

49:03.960 --> 49:05.560
Uh, they said I could stay.

49:06.560 --> 49:09.760
I know, this is preposterous.

49:10.520 --> 49:12.680
Plenty of other rooms to stay in.

49:17.320 --> 49:19.560
-Goodnight, Mr. Oliver.
-You have my card.

49:20.600 --> 49:22.160
Anytime you're in London,

49:22.920 --> 49:24.920
we could have tea.

49:59.920 --> 50:01.160
ARTHUR: I went looking for you.

50:04.240 --> 50:05.760
I thought you'd be in here.

50:07.160 --> 50:08.280
I knew it.

50:09.560 --> 50:11.640
I wanted to end with a bit of peace.

50:12.280 --> 50:13.440
(WHISPERS) Yeah.

50:15.040 --> 50:16.200
Look what I found.

50:18.240 --> 50:20.880
It's beautiful. Thanks.

50:32.160 --> 50:35.240
Arthur, you mustn't worry about
what happened with the speech.

50:40.560 --> 50:43.840
What was in your heart was beautiful.

50:49.360 --> 50:51.960
God hears all the speeches
that don't get said.

50:55.840 --> 50:59.280
And isn't it nice to still be yourself
at this time of night?

51:04.520 --> 51:07.520
Close your eyes, Arthur,
and spend a minute thinking about that.

51:11.080 --> 51:12.760
(MUSIC PLAYING)

51:32.200 --> 51:34.080
(BABY CRYING)

51:34.160 --> 51:35.680
TOMMY: It's all right.

51:35.760 --> 51:36.960
It's all right.

51:49.920 --> 51:50.960
(SHUSHING)

53:05.600 --> 53:06.720
(INAUDIBLE)

53:52.720 --> 53:54.600
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

54:35.920 --> 54:40.080
More money than all those
fucking toffs put together, eh?

54:41.440 --> 54:44.480
And you're willing to gamble it all
on one robbery.

54:46.240 --> 54:47.880
I'm a gambling man, Pol.

54:48.960 --> 54:50.960
(THEME SONG PLAYING)
